0:     * 【95†7.77. CUpti_ActivityMemoryPool】\nL101:     * 【96†7.78. CUpti_ActivityMemoryPool2】\nL102:     * 【97†7.79. CUpti_ActivityMemoryPool3】\nL103:     * 【98†7.80. CUpti_ActivityMemset】\nL104:     * 【99†7.81. CUpti_ActivityMemset2】\nL105:     * 【100†7.82. CUpti_ActivityMemset3】\nL106:     * 【101†7.83. CUpti_ActivityMemset4】\nL107:     * 【102†7.84. CUpti_ActivityMetric】\nL108:     * 【103†7.85. CUpti_ActivityMetricInstance】\nL109:     * 【104†7.86. CUpti_ActivityModule】\nL110:     * 【105†7.87. CUpti_ActivityName】\nL111:     * 【106†7.88. CUpti_ActivityNvLink】\nL112:     * 【107†7.89. CUpti_ActivityNvLink2】\nL113:     * 【108†7.90. CUpti_ActivityNvLink3】\nL114:     * 【109†7.91. CUpti_ActivityNvLink4】\nL115:     * 【110†7.92. CUpti_ActivityNvLink5】\nL116:     * 【111†7.93. CUpti_ActivityObjectKindId】\nL117:     * 【112†7.94. CUpti_ActivityOpenAcc】\nL118:     * 【113†7.95. CUpti_ActivityOpenAccData】\nL119:     * 【114†7.96. CUpti_ActivityOpenAccLaunch】\nL120:     * 【115†7.97. CUpti_ActivityOpenAccOther】\nL121:     * 【116†7.98. CUpti_ActivityOpenMp】\nL122:     * 【117†7.99. CUpti_ActivityOverhead】\nL123:     * 【118†7.100. CUpti_ActivityOverhead2】\nL124:     * 【119†7.101. CUpti_ActivityOverhead3】\nL125:     * 【120†7.102. CUpti_ActivityOverheadCommandBufferFullData】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nReleases · Consensys-Incorporated/gnark · GitHub (https://github.com/Consensys/gnark/releases)\nciteturn3view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn1view2\",\"pattern\":\"same-degree\"}); Redirected to URL: https://github.com/Consensys-Incorporated/gnark/releases; Total lines: 1191\nL195: ### Hardening via gnark-crypto\nL196: \nL197:   * `field/extensions`: the vector length read by `AsyncReadFrom` is now bounded, which prevents excessive allocation from crafted input (【78†Consensys-Incorporated/gnark-crypto#878】).\nL198: \nL199: * * *\nL200: \nL201: ## 💥 Breaking changes\nL202: ### Circuits: constraint systems change, so a new setup is needed\nL203: \nL204: Several gadgets now produce different constraint systems. If your circuit uses any of the gadgets below, recompile it. For Groth16, run a new circuit-specific setup and redeploy on-chain verifiers, because proving and verifying keys from v0.16.3 will not work. Constraint systems serialized with an older version must also be recompiled.\nL205: Area  | Change  | PR\nL206: --- | --- | ---\nL207: Emulated scalar mul (secp256k1, BN254, P-256, P-384, STARK)  | on-curve check on the hinted result  | 【73†GHSA-7fx8-hmgc-82jp】\nL208: Emulated `AddUnified` on j ≠ 0 curves (P-256, P-384, STARK)  | new slope selection  | 【73†GHSA-7fx8-hmgc-82jp】\nL209: Emulated fixed-base scalar mul (comb)  | optimal window: R1CS w = 9/10, PLONK w = 6  | 【79†#1826】\nL210: Emulated 4D GLV+fakeGLV, BN254/BLS12-381 G2 scalar mul  | tighter subscalar bound  | 【79†#1826】\nL211: BLS12-381 G1 `AssertIsOnG1` / subgroup check  | `[x-1]`-preimage check replaces Bowe's endomorphism test  | 【79†#1826】\nL212: BW6-761 `AssertFinalExponentiationIsOne`  | non-zero residue witness  | 【74†#1871】\nL213: BW6-761 pairing (emulated)  | supports G1 point at infinity (+74 R1CS / +145 SCS)  | 【80†#1850】\nL214: BLS12-377 pairing (native, in BW6-761)  | supports G1 point at infinity (+4 R1CS / +7 SCS)  | 【81†#1851】\nL215: Groth16 recursive verifier  | complete addition for `K[0]`  | 【82†#1843】\nL216: Keccak-f[1600] permutation (SHA3/Keccak gadgets)  | new permutation circuit  | 【83†#1802】\nL217: `std/math/uints` byte ops  | constant folding of `And`/`Or`/`Xor`  | 【84†#1796】\nL218: ### Go toolchain: Go 1.26 is now required\nL219: \nL220: `go.mod` now declares `go 1.26.8` (【85†#1866】). Projects building with Go 1.25 must upgrade their toolchain.\nL221: ### API changes\nL222:   * Removed `backend/plonk/bn254.UnmarshalSolidity`, which was stale and no longer matched the proof layout (【86†#1839】).\nL223:   * GKR: the native GKR prover and verifier are now public in `gkr/<curve>` (previously `internal/gkr/<curve>`). The gate API (`Variable`, `GateAPI`, `GateFunction`, `GateName`) moved to the `gkr` package. The `std/gkrapi/gkr` names remain as type aliases (【87†#1852】, 【88†#1844】).\nL224:   * GKR proof format: the default scheduler now batches same-degree zero-checks into one sum-check level, and the Fiat–Shamir binding of the final evaluation proof changed. GKR proofs and schedules from earlier versions are not compatible (【89†#1828】).\nL225:   * `sw_emulated.CurveParams` has a new field `PrimeOrder`. `AssertIsInSubgroup` is now exported. It panics at circuit-definition time if a curve has neither `PrimeOrder: true` nor a `CofactorClearing` constant, instead of silently doing nothing. If you build `CurveParams` literals for your own prime-order curve, set `PrimeOrder: true` (【79†#1826】).\nL226:   * Emulated hints: `unifiedSlopeHint` takes an optional fifth input (curve coefficient `a`), and `bjSlopeHint` was removed. This only matters if you run a custom hint registry or solver.\nL227: * * *\nL228: ## Highlights\nL229: ### ✨ Features\nL230:   * WebGPU + WASM proving backend for PLONK and Groth16 over BN254, BLS12-377 and BLS12-381. This is experimental (【90†#1789】, 【91†#1832】).\nL231:   * Public GKR prover/verifier API for use outside gnark (【87†#1852】, 【88†#1844】). The GKR scheduler now batches sum-checks (【89†#1828】).\nL232:   * `bits.ToBinary` has a new `WithUpperBound` option to tighten the decomposition bound for values known to be small (【92†#1809】).\nL233:   * EdDSA `Assign` helpers support Bandersnatch (BLS12-381), and Bandersnatch EdDSA tests are enabled again (【93†#1818】).\nL234: ### 🚀 Performance\nL235: \nL236:   * Emulated scalar multiplication (【79†#1826】):\nL237:     * optimal comb window for fixed-base scalar mul, chosen per curve and backend\nL238:     * tighter subscalar bound for the 4D GLV+fakeGLV decomposition (one fewer loop iteration)\nL239:     * cheaper BLS12-381 G1 subgroup check (64-bit `[x-1]` ladder instead of a 128-bit one)\nL240:   * Keccak-f[1600] permutation optimizations (【83†#1802】)\nL241:   * Compile-time folding of constant byte operations in `std/math/uints` (【84†#1796】)\nL242: ### 🐛 Fixes\nL243:   * Groth16 recursive verifier rejected valid proofs when the inner circuit had no public inputs or all public inputs were zero (【82†#1843】)\nL244:   * BW6-761 and BLS12-377 pairings failed on a G1 point at infinity (【80†#1850】, 【81†#1851】)\nL245:   * R1CS `Commit` panicked when a later commitment reused a variable that an earlier commitment already covered (【94†#1814】)\nL246:   * `Witness.FromJSON` modified the caller's schema in place (【95†#1821】)\nL247:   * `profile.Top()` reported operations instead of constraints (【96†#1835】)\nL248: ### 📝 Documentation\nL249: \nL250:   * Security assumptions of precomputed G2 lines (【77†#1858】) and KZG point-evaluation limb ranges (【76†#1863】)\nL251:   * Security reporting addresses (【97†#1829】)\nL252: \nL253: ### 📦 Dependencies\nL254: \nL255:   * gnark-crypto `v0.21.1-0.20260913224755-1409fe592052` (【98†Consensys-Incorporated/gnark-crypto@`1409fe592`】, also included in gnark-crypto v0.22.0)\nL256:   * Go 1.26 (【85†#1866】)\nL257: ## New Contributors\nL258: \nL259:   * 【99†@ginavalent】 made their first contribution in 【95†#1821】\nL260:   * 【100†@rdubois-crypto】 made their first contribution in 【93†#1818】\nL261:   * 【101†@Bruce039】 made their first contribution in 【96†#1835】\nL262:   * 【102†@FlashWayne】 made their first contribution in 【82†#1843】\nL263:   * 【103†@colinaumaty】 made their first contribution in 【91†#1832】\nL264:   * 【104†@zexoverz】 made their first contribution in 【92†#1809】\nL265:   * 【105†@colll】...\nL266: \nL267: 【66†Read more】\nL268: ### Contributors\nL269: \nL270:   *   *   *   *   *   *   * colll78, zexoverz, and 5 other contributors\nL271: \nL272: Assets 2\nL273: \nL274: Loading\nL275: \nL276: ### Uh oh!\nL277: \nL278: There was an error while loading. Please reload this page.\nL279: \nL2